[:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Under the shadow of Windsor Castle, the race was 17 laps in " [:a {:href "/venues/343"} "Windsor Great Park"] ", on a relatively flat 11.45 km course. The event had not originally been intended for Windsor, but was to be held at Richmond Park, in Surrey.  However, a law was discovered that prohibited any activity there at more than 20 miles per hour, so the event had to be moved to Windsor. The race started in a torrential downpour, which limited the spectators, who braved the weather. The biggest problem with the course was the loose gravel roads, which caused over 100 punctures in all."] "\n\n" [:p {} "It was difficult to pick a favorite as international racing had been stalled by the war. The 1947 World Championships had been won by Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/14314"} "Alfo Ferrari"] ", who raced at Windsor, but trailed in only in 9th place, the leader of the chasing group. On the second lap of the race, three riders – " [:a {:href "/athletes/14925"} "Nils Johansson"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/17105"} "Gerrit Voorting"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/14397"} "Henk Faanhof"] " – dropped the peloton. Johansson punctured on the 9th lap and was caught by the pack. On the 12th lap, a group of nine riders caught the leading pair. Two punctures and a crash left a group of eight leading riders to contest the final lap. On the last lap, shortly before the top of Breakheart Hill, a short climb of no more than 25 metres elevation, " [:a {:href "/athletes/13598"} "José Beyaert"] " broke away and opened up a gap of eight bike lengths with less than 800 metres remaining.  He was not caught and won the gold medal, with Voorting outsprinting the group to win the silver medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In 1947, Beyaert had won Paris-Briare, and finished eighth at the World Championships. He had only finished third in the French selection race for the 1948 Olympics, but he had had a solid year, finishing second at Paris-Cayeux, Paris-Briare, and Paris-Saint-Valéry."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Margin"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/13598"} "José Beyaert"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "5-18:12.6"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/17105"} "Gerrit Voorting"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "at 0:03.6"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/17211"} "Lode Wouters"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "at 0:03.6"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/14122"} "Leon De Lathouwer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "at 0:03.6"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/14925"} "Nils Johansson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "http